00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:57,780
I think maybe the projector has overheated.

253
00:12:58,220 --> 00:13:00,960
We might need to cool it down for 10 minutes and start again.

254
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:03,200
I'll call IT support to come over right now.

255
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:04,700
Okay, guys.

256
00:13:05,460 --> 00:13:08,900
Unfortunately, technical problems do crop up from time to time, don't they?

257
00:13:09,310 --> 00:13:10,690
But it's not a huge problem.

258
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:21,240
In the meantime, while the IT guys get to work on that, I can talk a little bit more about the advertising concept and what we're looking to achieve overall with this campaign.

259
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:24,960
All right.

260
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:28,020
So this was part seven of our presentation series.

261
00:13:28,260 --> 00:13:34,880
And actually, these type of problems occur very, very often, specifically with the laptop and the projector.

262
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,720
And sometimes it doesn't work.

263
00:13:36,720 --> 00:13:37,940
It doesn't recognize it.

264
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:40,440
And so this is a nice way of handling it.

265
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:41,100
This is.

266
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:44,600
And we hope that these are phrases that you can use in your daily life as well.

267
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:48,320
Maybe you're working with your colleagues and you're having some technical problems.

268
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:52,360
Or if you're having a problem and someone gives you instructions for how to solve that problem.

269
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:55,100
Like, I often get this from my technical team.

270
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,280
I say, listen, I have a problem.

271
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:59,970
And they say, hey, just reboot your computer and it will be okay.

272
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:07,600
So these are very, very common issues that I think that you can learn how to describe in English with today's lesson.

273
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:07,770
All right.

274
